    {
      "type": "group",
      "name": "🇲🇬 Water quality Sentinel-2 — Madagascar central highlands",
      "description": "Chlorophyll-a and turbidity time series derived from Sentinel-2 (Terrascope/VITO) over the water bodies of Madagascar's central highlands, as daily, monthly and annual Cloud Optimized GeoTIFFs.",
      "isOpen": true,
      "members": [
        {
          "type": "cog-time-series",
          "id": "mdg-chl",
          "name": "Chlorophyll-a (CHL) — Madagascar central highlands",
          "description": "Chlorophyll-a (mg m-3) from Sentinel-2, 2015–2026, for the two MGRS tiles Terrascope (VITO) processes over Madagascar's central highlands (38KPD, 38KQD): Lake Itasy, the Mantasoa and Tsiazompaniry reservoirs, the Antsirabe lakes and reaches of the Sakay, Mania, Kitsamby and Onive rivers. MDN algorithm (Pahlevan et al. 2020), Terrascope collection terrascope-s2-chl-v1, 20 m.<br/><br/>Switch between <strong>Annual</strong>, <strong>Monthly</strong> and <strong>Daily</strong> on the workbench, pick a <strong>statistic</strong>, and use <strong>Go to a place</strong> to jump to a water body and chart it. Click any water pixel to chart its time series; click more to compare.<br/><br/><strong>How the values are built.</strong> Monthly = per-pixel statistics over the satellite passes of the month; the median is the reference because concentrations are log-normal. Annual = statistics over the <em>monthly medians</em> (each month weighs the same), because clear scenes concentrate in the dry season and averaging passes would bias the year towards it. Check <em>Months with data</em> before comparing years: 2015 (from October) and 2026 (to June) are partial. Indicative trophic classes (Carlson/OECD): oligotrophic < 2.6, mesotrophic 2.6–7.3, eutrophic 7.3–56, hypereutrophic > 56 mg m⁻³.<br/><br/>The colour scale is roughly logarithmic. Land, cloud and shadow are already masked by the provider.",
          "unit": "mg m-3",
          "opacity": 1,
