        {
          "type": "cog-time-series",
          "id": "mdg-tur",
          "name": "Turbidity (TUR) — Madagascar central highlands",
          "description": "Turbidity (FNU) from Sentinel-2, 2015–2026, for the two MGRS tiles Terrascope (VITO) processes over Madagascar's central highlands (38KPD, 38KQD): Lake Itasy, the Mantasoa and Tsiazompaniry reservoirs, the Antsirabe lakes and reaches of the Sakay, Mania, Kitsamby and Onive rivers. Dogliotti et al. (2015), Terrascope collection terrascope-s2-tur-v1, 10 m. The product saturates at 5000 FNU.<br/><br/>Switch between <strong>Annual</strong>, <strong>Monthly</strong> and <strong>Daily</strong> on the workbench, pick a <strong>statistic</strong>, and use <strong>Go to a place</strong> to jump to a water body and chart it. Click any water pixel to chart its time series; click more to compare.<br/><br/><strong>How the values are built.</strong> Monthly = per-pixel statistics over the satellite passes of the month; the median is the reference because concentrations are log-normal. Annual = statistics over the <em>monthly medians</em> (each month weighs the same), because clear scenes concentrate in the dry season and averaging passes would bias the year towards it. Check <em>Months with data</em> before comparing years: 2015 (from October) and 2026 (to June) are partial. Operational (not regulatory) classes: clear < 5, moderate 5–25, turbid 25–100, very turbid > 100 FNU.<br/><br/>The colour scale is roughly logarithmic. Land, cloud and shadow are already masked by the provider.",
